    "title": "Shapiro Administration Follows Through on Benninghoff Request for Increase in Statewide Truck Parking",
    "url": "https://www.kerrybenninghoff.com/News/37386/Press-Releases/Shapiro-Administration-Follows-Through-on-Benninghoff-Request-for-Increase-in-Statewide-Truck-Parking",
    "date": null,
    "raw_text": "Shapiro Administration Follows Through on Benninghoff Request for Increase in Statewide Truck Parking\nJanuary 28, 2026\nHARRISBURG – State Rep. Kerry Benninghoff (R-Centre/Mifflin), Republican chairman of the House Transportation Committee, is applauding efforts by PennDOT to increase available parking for Pennsylvania’s truck drivers.\n“Pennsylvania’s location lends itself to a high volume of interstate truck traffic, and the Federal Motor Carrier Safety Administration Hours of Service rules often require long-haul drivers to abruptly stop their journeys to be in compliance,” Benninghoff said. “The lack of significant truck parking often leads to competition among drivers for the existing spots, a problem further complicated by distribution centers not allowing truckers to stay on their property if they arrive early with their load.”\nTo address a decades-old problem, Benninghoff authored legislation early last year that would give businesses a tax credit for building additional truck parking spaces. While his bill sits with the House Finance Committee, Benninghoff is glad to see the problem begin to be addressed.\n“\nHouse Bill 709\nwould also require the Department of General Services to conduct a study in relation to truck parking statewide,” added Benninghoff. “It’s a safety issue for drivers who are moving valuable goods across our state and our country, and I’m glad to see the governor act on a problem my legislation brought to light.”\nOn Wednesday, the Shapiro administration formally announced the opening of 24 truck parking spaces which took place late last year, and a plan to open at least 1,200 more spaces by the end of this year.\nQuestions about this or any legislative issue should be directed to Benninghoff’s Bellefonte district office at 814-355-1300 or his Reedsville office at 717-667-1175.\nRepresentative Kerry Benninghoff\n171st Legislative District\nPennsylvania House of Representatives\nMedia Contact: Scott Little\n717-260-6137\nSlittle@pahousegop.com\nKerryBenninghoff.com / Facebook.com/RepBenninghoff\nShare\nSign Up to Receive Legislative Email Updates\nKeep up-to-date on the latest legislative and community news. Your email address will be used strictly for legislative purposes.\nEmail*\nZIP Code\nSubscribe",
